This is a fascinating collection because it isn't one game idea—it's actually **several generations of game ideas layered together**:

* Family life simulation (K)
* Pirate strategy and adventure (M)
* Tropical relaxation and exploration (Wifey)
* Dinosaurs and creatures (S)
* Civilization-building, exploration, science, mystery, and space travel (You)

Instead of choosing between them, I'd preserve all of them and build a universe where they naturally fit together.

# Core Design Philosophy

### "Live Any Life. Discover A Bigger World."

Players are never forced into a single gameplay style.

Someone can:

* Run a farm
* Raise children
* Become a pirate
* Hunt sea monsters
* Study chemistry
* Build factories
* Explore ancient ruins
* Tame dinosaurs
* Become a merchant
* Discover lost civilizations
* Build spacecraft
* Join kingdoms
* Become famous
* Become feared

The main story exists, but life exists outside the main story.

This preserves K's favorite part of Stardew Valley.

---

# The Universe

## The Great World of Ages

Most people believe they live in the entire world.

They are wrong.

The known world is called:

### The Inner Realm

A massive continent-and-ocean civilization where most humans live.

This is where new players begin.

The Inner Realm contains:

* towns
* farms
* kingdoms
* villages
* ports
* cities
* merchants
* schools
* guilds

Combat exists but is uncommon.

Many players may spend hundreds of hours here and never leave.

---

# Life Gameplay

Inspired by the ideas K loves.

Players can:

* marry
* date
* have children
* adopt children
* make friends
* own businesses
* own farms
* own ships
* own houses
* own castles
* decorate homes
* host festivals
* attend festivals
* raise animals

NPCs remember actions.

Different relationships unlock:

* quests
* recipes
* technologies
* companions
* story branches

No two playthroughs are identical.

---

# Seasons

The world has real seasonal cycles.

Spring:

* planting
* festivals
* migrations

Summer:

* sailing
* tropical exploration
* fishing

Autumn:

* harvesting
* storms

Winter:

* snow travel
* ice resources
* frozen expeditions

Some resources only exist during certain seasons.

