# Age System

One of the strongest ideas in your notes.

The world progresses through Ages.

Examples:

### Age of Giants

Massive creatures ruled.

### Age of Dragons

Flying civilizations.

### Age of Sail

Pirates and kingdoms.

### Age of Machines

Industrial powers.

### Age of Stars

Space civilization.

Each realm contains remnants of a former Age.

Players uncover how each Age ended.

---

# Why The Realms Are Isolated

This solves many design issues.

Long ago:

A catastrophic event called

## The Sundering

separated civilizations.

Travel became nearly impossible.

Each realm evolved independently.

This explains:

* dinosaurs surviving elsewhere
* different technologies
* different cultures
* different powers

without breaking immersion.

---

# The Great Resource

A mysterious substance connects all Ages.

Possible names:

* Aetherstone
* Star Iron
* Worldglass
* Genesis Ore

This material exists everywhere.

Different civilizations discovered different uses.

Examples:

Pirates:

* navigation

Dinosaurs:

* biological adaptation

Fantasy civilizations:

* magical effects

Scientists:

* advanced technology

Space civilizations:

* starship engines

This becomes the thread connecting every storyline.

